## Context

The author ruled on 2026-09-16 (recorded in 0909's body, "The canonical roots live in
`~/.idh`") that the harness project's own memory and the collective memory both stay
central in `~/.idh`, separated from each other. The v7 §12.1 disjoint-roots row stays
red until the repository itself leaves `~/.claude`, which is Claude Code's native config
and memory root. 0909 names the relocation as "the remaining half" of that row and
assigns it to the memory programme — but it never received its own ticket; this is it.

The 2026-09-28 amendment to 0800 sharpens the case: the repository being one runtime's
config directory is Claude-shaped, and every added target runtime (Codex, Pi, Vibe)
multiplies the ambiguity. Relocation makes `~/.idh` no runtime's native root.

Existing probes (0909 log, 2026-09-16): Claude Code follows a symlinked `rules/` and a
symlinked `CLAUDE.md`, both confirmed with positive controls. The memory probe's own
control did not fire, so it is recorded as an invalid probe rather than a negative;
the experiment that would settle it is named there.

## Relevant files

- `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md`, `STATE.md` — installation and location claims
- `scripts/path_utils.py` and the `IDH_ROOT` from-loaded-skill seam (ad33697b; 0803's
  territory) — what already tolerates a relocated root
- `tickets/0909-*.erg` — the ruling and the disjoint-roots row this closes
- `tickets/0920-*.erg`, `tickets/0923-*.erg` — siblings that still assert the store
  cannot leave `~/.claude`

## Actions

1. Decide the mechanism for Claude Code, which requires `~/.claude`: whole-directory
   symlink `~/.claude -> ~/.idh`, per-entry symlinks, or a projection. Extend the 0909
   probes with positive controls to hooks, `settings.json`, skills, commands and
   plugins before choosing; record what the runtime demonstrably follows.
2. Enumerate every tracked file and doc that names `~/.claude` as the canonical
   location before moving anything.
3. Execute the move with the repository clean and no other work in flight; document a
   tested rollback (restore the pointer).
4. Verify each runtime still finds the harness; record per-runtime evidence.
5. Update STATE.md's standing red row and the siblings' premise (0920, 0923).

## Test

Positive control: a fresh Claude Code session after the move loads hooks, skills,
`CLAUDE.md` and memory exactly as before. Negative control: breaking the pointer
produces a visible failure, not a silent fall-back to defaults.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The repository lives at `~/.idh`; `~/.claude` is a documented pointer that
      Claude Code demonstrably follows
- [ ] `make check` and the full suite pass after the move
- [ ] No tracked file names `~/.claude` as the canonical location without saying why
- [ ] The disjoint-roots row in 0909 turns green or carries its remaining condition
